9. Why AOP Doesn't Work for Internal Method Calls
Problem
@Service
class UserService {

    public void methodA() {
        methodB();   // AOP won't trigger
    }

    @LogExecution
    public void methodB() {}
}

Why? Spring AOP uses Proxy Objects.

Internal calls:
this.methodB(); -- bypass the proxy.

Solution 1 (Recommended) - Move logic to another bean.

@Service
class ValidatorService {}

@Service
class UserService {
    @Autowired
    ValidatorService validator;
}

Solution 2 - Self Injection
@Autowired
@Lazy
private UserService self;

Then:
self.methodB();

